1
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:21,240
System call.

2
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:23,060
Generate Luminous Element.

3
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:32,610
it.

4
00:00:32,693 --> 00:00:33,617
Wow, look at all this stuff.

5
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,237
Hurry, let's find our
swords and get out of here.

6
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:37,260
There They are?

7
00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:55,046
I can leave the room if
you two need a minute.

8
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:56,870
Sorry.

9
00:00:58,120 --> 00:00:59,320
I don't get it.

10
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:03,717
I thought the Integrity Knights were
enough to stop the forces of darkness.

11
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:05,840
Is the church building an army?

12
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:08,180
It's not that.

13
00:01:08,540 --> 00:01:10,128
It's the opposite, in fact.

14
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:13,837
The church brought all this here
to make sure no one builds one.

15
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:16,500
What would be the point of that? Simple.

16
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:19,537
The church doesn't want
people rising up against it.

17
00:01:19,620 --> 00:01:22,520
Or, to be more specific,
administrator doesn't.

18
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:25,997
Come on, let's get out of here.

19
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:27,021
Time's a-wasted.

20
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:30,000
Yeah, right. I'm coming.

21
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:34,377
Maybe we should take some armor.

22
00:01:34,460 --> 00:01:35,519
What do you think?

23
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:39,277
We never fought in it before,
so it might slow us down.

24
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:41,713
It's better if we stick to what we know.

25
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:44,748
We could use a fresh
set of clothes, though.

26
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:10,697
Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah.

27
00:02:10,780 --> 00:02:11,680
Oh, yeah.

28
00:02:13,740 --> 00:02:14,570
It's hard to say it.

29
00:02:14,653 --> 00:02:17,260
On the way, I'm going to step in.

30
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:20,490
Oh.

31
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:24,690
Oh, yeah.

32
00:02:24,773 --> 00:02:27,779
I don't know what you're
doing to tell you about it.

33
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:33,060
I don't know if you're gonna have a rule.

34
00:02:42,020 --> 00:02:43,257
Thank

35
00:02:43,340 --> 00:02:44,577
you

36
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:51,660
so

37
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:03,379
much for watching.

38
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:50,120
First element!

39
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:57,120
Charge him!

40
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:00,240
Futile.

41
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:19,660
Kirito! You hit?

42
00:04:22,340 --> 00:04:24,400
No. I'm good.

43
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:26,440
That was way too close.

44
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:35,420
Let's go.

45
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:36,920
System call.

46
00:04:45,100 --> 00:04:47,020
Uh-oh, not good.

47
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:48,880
That's no typical spell.

48
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:50,880
It's perfect weapon control.

49
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:53,320
Enhance armament.

50
00:05:14,940 --> 00:05:16,700
That bow's awesome!

51
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:19,500
Holy hell, I wonder what it was before.

52
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:22,056
We have bigger things to worry about.

53
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:27,160
I last bathed in the conflagration
bow's fire two years ago.

54
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:31,940
Now I summon the fire again
to deal with you sinners.

55
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:38,060
You have the skills to match Sir Eldrie,
but what you did to him is unforgivable.

56
00:05:38,780 --> 00:05:41,368
Instead of fighting
like knights with honor,

57
00:05:41,580 --> 00:05:46,620
you corrupted his mind and led him
astray with the Dark Arts. What?

58
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:48,117
It was nothing like that.

59
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:49,377
You're wrong, Sir Knight.

60
00:05:49,460 --> 00:05:53,217
All we did was remind him of his
life before he became a knight.

61
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:55,060
What are you babbling about?

62
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:57,277
We knights do not have a past.

63
00:05:57,360 --> 00:06:00,160
We have always been Integrity Knights.

64
00:06:00,540 --> 00:06:04,011
Our existence begins when we
are summoned from the heavens.

65
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:11,260
I should burn you criminals to ash,
but my orders are to capture you alive.

66
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:15,096
Unfortunately, I have unleashed
the conflagration bow.

67
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:19,080
Now one of your arms will
most likely be incinerated.

68
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:29,920
That bow's going to do serious damage now.

69
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:31,340
Any ideas?

70
00:06:31,860 --> 00:06:34,680
I got a feeling you can't
rapid-fire with that.

71
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:38,096
If I'm lucky and block the
first shot, you charge him.

72
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:39,820
That's not reassuring.

73
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:50,390
I'm ready.

74
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:05,460
System call!

75
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:07,460
Generate cryogenic elements!

76
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:11,020
Disharge!

77
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:15,280
Fool!

78
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:32,260
Oh, my God.

79
00:07:57,680 --> 00:07:58,510
Okay.

80
00:08:09,580 --> 00:08:10,410
Kirito!

81
00:08:13,320 --> 00:08:15,380
Now's your chance! Go get him!

82
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:26,000
Do not toy with me.

83
00:08:30,700 --> 00:08:31,620
Now what?

84
00:08:33,420 --> 00:08:37,185
You have to think about what
you're putting behind your strikes.

85
00:08:38,340 --> 00:08:41,157
What do you think I should
put behind mine, then?

86
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:44,828
That's something you're going
to have to figure out yourself.

87
00:08:56,020 --> 00:08:56,850
That's it.

88
00:08:57,260 --> 00:08:58,613
She's all that matters.

89
00:08:58,900 --> 00:09:01,500
I'm here for her, and
nothing will stop me.

90
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:06,260
Blue Rose Sword, lend me your power.

91
00:09:07,560 --> 00:09:10,600
Please, give me the
strength to keep going!

92
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:39,180
Please, you're cold and sharp.

93
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:44,300
Forged since creation by freezing cold
blizzards at the top of the End Mountains.

94
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:50,480
You can't let these weak flames melt.

95
00:09:50,980 --> 00:09:52,360
You, now!

96
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:16,520
You're finished!

97
00:10:31,520 --> 00:10:33,900
Oh, my God.

98
00:11:12,900 --> 00:11:17,120
Boy, that first skill
you used, what was it?

99
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:19,400
It's of the Aincrad style.

100
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:20,780
A two-hit strike.

101
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:22,160
Vertical arc.

102
00:11:22,540 --> 00:11:24,060
A two-hit strike.

103
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:30,897
And you what was your
skill Kirito are you okay

104
00:11:30,980 --> 00:11:34,340
yeah i'm good i healed
the worst burns myself

105
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:38,397
What's my skill it's
Aincrad too one of the

106
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:41,240
defense skills it's called spinning shield

107
00:11:44,220 --> 00:11:50,837
I thought i had seen it all i've been from
one end of this realm to the other And

108
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:57,100
beyond and yet there are styles i've never
seen and skills i've never encountered

109
00:11:58,200 --> 00:12:02,117
I can tell there is much
discipline in you and

110
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:04,906
you have spent years of
training in your style

111
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:09,057
Earlier i accused you
of using the dark arts

112
00:12:09,140 --> 00:12:13,760
to corrupt Sir Eldrie
i know now that i was

113
00:12:14,340 --> 00:12:15,170
mistaken.

114
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:18,000
I would be honored to know your names.

115
00:12:18,480 --> 00:12:21,037
I am Eugeo, the swordsman.

116
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:22,355
Kirito the swordsman.

117
00:12:26,380 --> 00:12:32,560
On the 50th floor, in the great hall of
ghostly light, Integrity Knights wait.

118
00:12:32,860 --> 00:12:34,200
Should you pass me,

119
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:37,557
they will not take you prisoner.

120
00:12:37,640 --> 00:12:40,800
They have orders to
extinguish your lives instead.

121
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:44,940
If you charge them head-on
like you did me just now,

122
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:47,580
you will most certainly meet your end.

123
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:49,500
Whoa, hang on a sec.

124
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:50,880
Why tell us?

125
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:52,394
Whose side are you on?

126
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:56,360
I failed to carry out
Administrator's order.

127
00:12:56,880 --> 00:13:02,040
I shall be stripped of my armor and
divine object, the proof of my knighthood.

128
00:13:02,700 --> 00:13:05,140
Then I shall be frozen for eternity.

129
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:09,280
I do not wish to suffer the indignity.

130
00:13:09,860 --> 00:13:14,260
Therefore, I want you to end my life.

131
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:17,900
There is no need to hesitate.

132
00:13:18,700 --> 00:13:22,940
After all, you defeated me fairly,
using your splendid skills.

133
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:28,880
By the way, my name is
Tiese Elbert Synthesis 7.

134
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:40,600
You're Tiese Elbert?

135
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:49,960
Yu-Gi-Oh, you're the one who took her.

136
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:00,980
A fair battle.

137
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:02,620
Dignity?

138
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:07,120
You want to die with honor, do you?

139
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:08,700
Do you?

140
00:14:09,680 --> 00:14:13,268
Where was your honor when you
chained up an 11-year-old girl?

141
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:16,380
You tied her to your
dragon and took her away.

142
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,880
Dying with honor is too good for you!

143
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:36,160
I'm right. I am.

144
00:14:36,400 --> 00:14:37,240
Aren't I?

145
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:39,180
You heard what he said.

146
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:41,206
He's not going to fight back.

147
00:14:41,300 --> 00:14:43,418
You don't kill a defenseless person.

148
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:48,037
I know, but...

149
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:50,640
he came to my village and took Alice!

150
00:15:02,620 --> 00:15:05,537
You know the church messes
with these guys' heads.

151
00:15:05,620 --> 00:15:09,340
I doubt he remembers being in
Rulid, or taking Alice away.

152
00:15:10,840 --> 00:15:12,240
It's true, ain't it?

153
00:15:12,540 --> 00:15:13,980
You don't remember.

154
00:15:21,300 --> 00:15:23,600
It is as your companion says.

155
00:15:24,060 --> 00:15:25,340
I am a knight.

156
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:26,710
I protect.

157
00:15:26,793 --> 00:15:31,460
I would never kidnap a child,
much less chain them to my dragon.

158
00:15:32,620 --> 00:15:34,580
If I did, I do not remember.

159
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:36,548
What are you talking about?

160
00:15:36,920 --> 00:15:39,060
It happened eight years ago!

161
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:42,400
Old man, I mean Tiese Elbert.

162
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:47,240
Eight years ago, you were guarding
the border of North Norlinggarth.

163
00:15:47,700 --> 00:15:49,200
Do you remember that?

164
00:15:50,260 --> 00:15:51,090
I do.

165
00:15:51,173 --> 00:15:53,580
District 7 in North Norlinggarth was mine.

166
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:56,240
I used to patrol the borderlands.

167
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:59,160
That is, until eight years ago.

168
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:03,660
For some reason, the church rewarded me.

169
00:16:04,620 --> 00:16:09,320
I received this armor and was given the
duty to guard the central cathedral.

170
00:16:09,740 --> 00:16:12,622
Do you remember what the
church rewarded you for?

171
00:16:14,740 --> 00:16:16,480
I'll tell you why you don't.

172
00:16:16,700 --> 00:16:19,540
You were on a mission to steal his friend.

173
00:16:19,820 --> 00:16:22,200
She's called Alice Synthesis 30 now.

174
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:26,657
As soon as you brought her back here,
Administrator rewarded you all right.

175
00:16:26,740 --> 00:16:29,600
She also erased your
memory of what you did,

176
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:32,177
because she can't have
you remembering her.

177
00:16:32,260 --> 00:16:35,960
You told us before that
Integrity Knights have no past.

178
00:16:36,220 --> 00:16:40,057
Your lives begin when you're summoned
from heaven, but that's a lie.

179
00:16:40,140 --> 00:16:43,037
That's something the Pontifex
tells all the Knights,

180
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:45,840
right after they come
to, and you know why?

181
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:48,897
To help explain why
none of you can remember

182
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:51,627
anything before becoming
an Integrity Knight.

183
00:16:53,060 --> 00:16:56,580
She doesn't want you to have
any memories, not even one.

184
00:16:56,740 --> 00:17:00,097
And she doesn't stop with the
memories of your human life.

185
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:03,121
She takes the ones you
have of other knights, too.

186
00:17:03,340 --> 00:17:05,811
The ones you brought to her to get turned.

187
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:08,537
If a sinner you brought
in for judgment showed up

188
00:17:08,620 --> 00:17:10,997
as a knight the next day
and you remembered them,

189
00:17:11,080 --> 00:17:12,300
there'd be chaos.

190
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:15,600
But I would remember. I would.

191
00:17:16,480 --> 00:17:19,520
Like I said, Administrator
stole your memories.

192
00:17:19,780 --> 00:17:22,940
And then, she forced
absolute loyalty on you.

193
00:17:23,240 --> 00:17:25,240
Then she turned you into a knight.

194
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:28,240
But you're human, just like us.

195
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:29,870
Human?

196
00:17:30,180 --> 00:17:32,460
And having my memory manipulated?

197
00:17:33,360 --> 00:17:34,820
By the Pontifex?

198
00:17:35,920 --> 00:17:36,750
Impossible.

199
00:17:37,440 --> 00:17:38,960
Absurd. No, boy.

200
00:17:39,980 --> 00:17:42,280
You are the one who is mistaken here.

201
00:17:42,740 --> 00:17:44,622
Look, try to remember something.

202
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:46,180
Anything at all.

203
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:48,871
I bet there's an image or a feeling there.

204
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:52,500
Something so precious to
you, no art can erase it.

205
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:59,500
From the time I first ascended,
I keep having the same dream.

206
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:05,620
A delicate hand shaking me awake,
and on one finger, a silver ring.

207
00:18:12,840 --> 00:18:16,460
And when I do wake up,
there's no one there.

208
00:18:19,380 --> 00:18:22,740
Whoever that hand belongs to
is someone special to you.

209
00:18:23,480 --> 00:18:25,774
Administrator stole your memory of him.

210
00:18:26,120 --> 00:18:28,200
What you do next is up to you.

211
00:18:28,940 --> 00:18:32,469
You can go back to Administrator
and accept your punishment.

212
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:35,340
Or you can heal yourself
and come after us.

213
00:18:35,920 --> 00:18:36,920
Your call.

214
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:11,377
All these stairs.

215
00:19:11,460 --> 00:19:13,100
How far up are we now?

216
00:19:13,940 --> 00:19:15,697
The next floor is the 29th.

217
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:19,780
At the rate we're going, we'll reach
the 50th floor in half an hour.

218
00:19:20,060 --> 00:19:21,531
Should we just charge in?

219
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:25,960
Good question.

220
00:19:29,540 --> 00:19:30,952
You think of everything.

221
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:40,977
After seeing how that last
dude fought, I got a theory.

222
00:19:41,060 --> 00:19:43,766
Combo attacks seem to
throw these knights off.

223
00:19:43,940 --> 00:19:46,822
It's like they never had
a deal with them before.

224
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:51,197
If it's one-on-one and we could get
up close, I think we'd have a chance.

225
00:19:51,280 --> 00:19:55,157
But that knight said there's a bunch
up there and they're ready for us.

226
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:57,137
That's going to make things harder.

227
00:19:57,220 --> 00:19:58,050
You're right.

228
00:19:58,160 --> 00:19:59,737
Perhaps we should avoid them.

229
00:19:59,820 --> 00:20:01,000
Find another way up.

230
00:20:01,420 --> 00:20:03,460
Yeah, I don't know about that.

231
00:20:04,280 --> 00:20:06,697
Cardinal said these stairs
were the only way up,

232
00:20:06,780 --> 00:20:09,037
so we're going to have to deal with them.

233
00:20:09,120 --> 00:20:13,708
Even if we did find a way around, we'd
have to face them on the way back down.

234
00:20:13,820 --> 00:20:15,797
We should deal with those knights now.

235
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:17,880
Our new special skill should help.

236
00:20:18,400 --> 00:20:19,230
That's right.

237
00:20:19,400 --> 00:20:20,753
Perfect weapon control.

238
00:20:21,860 --> 00:20:22,690
Yup.

239
00:20:22,773 --> 00:20:27,021
Maybe if we use it when we charge in, we
can take a bunch out before they can react.

240
00:20:27,340 --> 00:20:30,281
With any luck, our first
strike will get them all.

241
00:20:31,020 --> 00:20:33,140
Actually, we should talk about that.

242
00:20:33,320 --> 00:20:35,202
I don't think I'll be much help.

243
00:20:35,320 --> 00:20:38,277
My version of perfect
weapon control isn't a

244
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:41,066
direct attack like that
Integrity Knights was.

245
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:42,330
What?

246
00:20:42,413 --> 00:20:43,243
You're kidding.

247
00:20:43,326 --> 00:20:44,156
Uh-uh.

248
00:20:44,239 --> 00:20:46,857
Not based on the command
Cardinal wrote for me.

249
00:20:46,940 --> 00:20:50,880
I mean, I guess in the end
it's my fault for imagining it.

250
00:20:51,280 --> 00:20:54,940
Well, let me check it out and
see what's up with it. Okay.

251
00:21:00,360 --> 00:21:01,478
Yeah, you're right.

252
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:04,680
It might not be quick enough
for a surprise attack.

253
00:21:04,780 --> 00:21:07,917
Still, it should come in handy
as long as you use it right.

254
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:11,177
Plus, it looks like it complements
my perfect control art.

255
00:21:11,260 --> 00:21:12,090
Really?

256
00:21:12,173 --> 00:21:13,786
Can I see what yours is like?

257
00:21:14,060 --> 00:21:16,413
Nah, I don't want to spoil the surprise.

258
00:21:21,740 --> 00:21:24,160
Let's get going. Huh?

259
00:21:37,220 --> 00:21:39,600
